Yes, 41 Burnside Lane is within the Burnside Conservation Area. It is not a listed building and has no tree preservation order.

The council's guidance says that replacement windows in a conservation area need a planning application, unless the new windows match the existing ones in material and pattern.

So before you go ahead, consider the following:
- If you want a different material (for example, uPVC instead of timber) or a different design or glazing pattern, you will likely need to apply.
- If the new windows are an exact match to the existing ones, you may not need an application. I can't confirm that for your specific case, though. The council will need to make that judgement, so it's worth asking the planning desk to confirm before you order.

If you have an existing application reference for work at this property, I can look up its status for you.
